<title>MEXICO: Fire forces evacuation of Mexican Stock Exchange.</title>
<headline>Fire forces evacuation of Mexican Stock Exchange.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Mexican Stock Exchange building was evacuated after trading closed on Thursday because of a small electrical fire, witnesses said.</p>
<p>&quot;It was an electrical substation in the basement,&quot; a security guard told Reuters.</p>
<p>There were no injuries reported.</p>
<p>Stock exchange employees and floor traders were gathered outside the building on Paseo de la Reforma, the main avenue of central Mexico City.</p>
<p>The small fire broke out at 3:10 p.m. (2010 GMT), 10 minutes after the close of trade.</p>
<p>((--Cyntia Barrera, Mexico City newsroom, +728-9549))</p>
